{
  "dom_id": "step-q94195",
  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\u03a6(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ compute $P(0.70<Z<0.92).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7580\\,$ | $\\,0.7611\\,$ | $\\,0.7642\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7881\\,$ | $\\,0.7910\\,$ | $\\,0.7939\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.8159\\,$ | $\\,0.8186\\,$ | $\\,0.8212\\,$ |",
  "worked_solution": "We're given that $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(0.70<Z<0.92).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/3eb46852c53e4fa13aaa29c31623153bfef604d138f15c6da67732d5730b785f.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $\u03a6(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=\u03a6(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $\u03a6(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.70<Z<0.92) & =P(Z<0.92)-P(Z\\le 0.70) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0.92)-P(Z\\le 0.70) \\\\  & =\u03a6(0.92)-\u03a6(0.70)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the tables, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u03a6(0.70) & =0.7580 \\\\ \u03a6(0.92) & =0.8212\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.7<Z<0.92) & =\u03a6(0.92)-\u03a6(0.70) \\\\  & =0.8212-0.7580 \\\\  & =0.0632.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
